<article class="env-lemma" id="0BCK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BCK">Lemma <span data-tag="0BCK">28.28.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a quasi-affine scheme. For any quasi-compact immersion $i : X' \to X$ the scheme $X'$ is quasi-affine. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This can be proved directly without making use of the material on ample invertible sheaves; we urge the reader to do this on a napkin. Since $X$ is quasi-affine, we have that $\mathcal{O}_ X$ is ample by Lemma <a href="/tag/01QE" data-tag="01QE">28.28.1</a>. Then $\mathcal{O}_{X'}$ is ample by Lemma <a href="/tag/0B3E" data-tag="0B3E">28.27.14</a>. Then $X'$ is quasi-affine by Lemma <a href="/tag/01QE" data-tag="01QE">28.28.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>